Source: ryzen-control
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: senseikiritof <tonifede98@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-sequence-dkms, python3
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/SenseiKiritof/Ryzen-Control
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: ryzen-control
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.9), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5), pkexec, polkitd,
 systemd, kmod
Recommends: stress-ng, libnotify-bin
Description: Ryzen Master-style control for AMD Ryzen desktop CPUs
 Per-core Curve Optimizer, PPT/TDC/EDC limits, boost frequency (FMax), maximum
 temperature, power profile and motherboard fans, with modes calibrated on the
 CPU, a GTK4/libadwaita GUI with a tray icon and a root helper (ryzenctl).
 Profiles are applied at boot, with protection after a crash. Includes the
 source of the ryzen_smu kernel module, built by DKMS.
